=== AW. 17 CFR 240.16a-7: Transactions effected in connection with a distribution ===
official caption typography is Transactions effected in connection with a distribution.
16a-7(a): Any purchase and sale, or sale and purchase, of a security that is made in connection with the distribution of a substantial block of securities shall be exempt from the provisions of section 16(a) of the Act, to the extent specified in this rule, subject to the following conditions:
16a-7(a)(1): The person effecting the transaction is engaged in the business of distributing securities and is participating in good faith, in the ordinary course of such business, in the distribution of such block of securities; and
16a-7(a)(2): The security involved in the transaction is:
16a-7(a)(2)(i): Part of such block of securities and is acquired by the person effecting the transaction, with a view to distribution thereof, from the issuer or other person on whose behalf such securities are being distributed or from a person who is participating in good faith in the distribution of such block of securities; or
16a-7(a)(2)(ii): A security purchased in good faith by or for the account of the person effecting the transaction for the purpose of stabilizing the market price of securities of the class being distributed or to cover an over-allotment or other short position created in connection with such distribution.
16a-7(b): Each person participating in the transaction must qualify on an individual basis for an exemption pursuant to this section.
